     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"line-height:1.38;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;Geneva&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nDear Julia,</div>\r\n<div style=\"line-height:1.38;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;Geneva&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"line-height:1.38;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;Geneva&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nsorry, but no. We are just not fans of online/hybrid courses. Admittedly, an online option would carry benefits for people who cannot physically attend. However, for us and for the people who do physically attend, it would entail substantial costs: having to\r\n cater for an online audience completely changes the whole character of a course as a lively event with direct interactions between humans. We do like this human side of a course very much, as it allows for far richer forms of communication and exchange.</div>\r\n<div style=\"line-height:1.38;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;Geneva&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"line-height:1.38;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;Geneva&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nBest regards  --- Marc</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;Geneva&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;Geneva&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nPS: &quot;mirrored over&quot; to the HMecology list as well</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;Geneva&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;Geneva&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;Geneva&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"